      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="auth">
        <h3 class="form-section">Authentication</h3>
        <p class="muted">Every endpoint — including the liveness probe — requires an API key created by a <b>FirmLedger Pro</b> account at <a href="/dashboard/api" style="color:var(--accent)">/dashboard/api</a>. Send it in the <code>Authorization</code> header — never in URLs or bodies. There are <b>no public endpoints</b>: key-less requests receive <code>401 missing_key</code>.</p>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">headers</span>Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key_here
<span class="c"># X-API-Key: fl_live_your_key_here   ← accepted alternative</span></div>
        <table class="facts">
          <tr><th>Key format</th><td><code>fl_live_</code> + 32 characters — shown once at creation, stored only as a SHA-256 hash</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Keys per account</th><td>Up to <strong><%= limits.MAX_KEYS %></strong> active — use one per integration, revoke instantly from the console</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Access requirement</th><td>An active <strong>FirmLedger Pro</strong> subscription — lapsed plans receive <code>403 pro_required</code> until renewal</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Failures</th><td>Unknown key → <code>401 invalid_key</code> · revoked → <code>401 key_revoked</code> · malformed → <code>401 invalid_key</code> (counted by the brute-force guard)</td></tr>
        </table>
        <h4 style="margin:22px 0 8px">Scopes</h4>
        <p class="muted">Keys can be narrowed per integration. Existing keys created before scopes were introduced retain full access. A missing permission returns <code>403 insufficient_scope</code> with <code>required_scope</code> in <code>error.details</code>.</p>
        <table class="facts">
          <tr><th><code>read:listings</code></th><td>Approved directory, profiles, directory filters, categories, countries, suggestions, domain verification and <code>GET /my/listings</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th><code>write:listings</code></th><td>Create, update and delete listing records you own</td></tr>
          <tr><th><code>export</code></th><td><code>GET /export/listings.csv</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th><code>manage:webhooks</code></th><td>Create, inspect, test, rotate and remove webhooks</td></tr>
          <tr><th><code>read:usage</code></th><td><code>/me</code> and <code>/usage</code>, including rate-limit snapshots</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="limits">
        <h3 class="form-section">Rate limits &amp; protection</h3>
        <p class="muted">Limits are per rolling 60-second window, per key. They exist to stop bots from hammering the record store and to keep one loud integration from slowing everyone else down.</p>
        <table class="facts">
          <tr><th>Reads (GET)</th><td><strong><%= limits.READ_RPM %> / minute</strong> per key</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Writes (POST · PUT · DELETE)</th><td><strong><%= limits.WRITE_RPM %> / minute</strong> per key, plus a platform-wide ceiling of <strong><%= limits.GLOBAL_WRITE_RPM %> writes / minute</strong></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Concurrency</th><td>Up to <strong><%= limits.MAX_INFLIGHT %></strong> simultaneous requests per key — beyond that, <code>429 too_many_concurrent</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Brute-force guard</th><td>After <strong><%= limits.BRUTE_MAX_FAILS %> invalid keys</strong> from one network address: <code>429 ip_locked</code> for <strong><%= limits.BRUTE_LOCK_MIN %> minutes</strong></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Body limit</th><td>JSON request bodies up to <strong>100 KB</strong> — larger gets <code>413 payload_too_large</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Write integrity</th><td>Every write is a single transaction (WAL journal, busy-timeout) — records can never half-save, and writes queue instead of stampeding</td></tr>
        </table>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-top:6px">Every response tells you where you stand — mind these headers before you retry:</p>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">rate-limit headers on every response</span><span class="k">X-RateLimit-Limit</span>: <span class="s"><%= limits.READ_RPM %></span>        <span class="c"># your window size (reads shown here)</span>
<span class="k">X-RateLimit-Remaining</span>: <span class="s">58</span>   <span class="c"># calls left in the current window</span>
<span class="k">X-RateLimit-Reset</span>: <span class="s">23</span>      <span class="c"># seconds until the window rolls</span>
<span class="k">X-RateLimit-Scope</span>: <span class="s">read</span>     <span class="c"># which budget this call consumed</span>
<span class="k">X-Request-Id</span>: <span class="s">req_1ab2c3d4e5f6a7b8</span>  <span class="c"># quote it when writing to support</span></div>
        <p class="fine-print">When you do hit a limit, the status is <code>429</code> and the <code>Retry-After</code> header (plus <code>error.retry_after_seconds</code>) tells you exactly when to try again. Honor it — clients that respect back-off are never permanently blocked.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="errors">
        <h3 class="form-section">Errors</h3>
        <p class="muted">Machine-readable envelope on every failure — same shape everywhere:</p>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">error shape</span>{
  <span class="k">"error"</span>: {
    <span class="k">"code"</span>: <span class="s">"validation_failed"</span>,
    <span class="k">"message"</span>: <span class="s">"Some fields need attention."</span>,
    <span class="k">"details"</span>: { <span class="k">"errors"</span>: [ { <span class="k">"field"</span>: <span class="s">"tagline"</span>, <span class="k">"message"</span>: <span class="s">"Required, 20–90 characters…"</span> } ] }
  }
}</div>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table class="table">
            <thead><tr><th>HTTP</th><th><code>error.code</code></th><th>Meaning &amp; fix</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>400</td><td><code>invalid_json</code> · <code>invalid_body</code> · <code>missing_query</code> · <code>invalid_domain</code></td><td>Body isn't valid JSON/object, or a required query/domain param is missing or malformed.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>401</td><td><code>missing_key</code> · <code>invalid_key</code> · <code>key_revoked</code></td><td>No/unknown/dead key. Create a fresh one in the console; revoked keys never come back.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>403</td><td><code>pro_required</code> · <code>account_suspended</code> · <code>insufficient_scope</code></td><td>Pro plan inactive, account suspended, or this key needs one of the documented scopes.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>404</td><td><code>not_found</code> · <code>unknown_endpoint</code></td><td>That listing/slug/domain isn't on the ledger, or the path/method isn't in v1.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>409</td><td><code>duplicate_listing</code> · <code>webhook_exists</code> · <code>webhook_limit</code></td><td>A record/domain or receiver URL already exists — <code>details.existing</code> carries listing identity where applicable.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>413</td><td><code>payload_too_large</code></td><td>Body over 100 KB — trim the description or split the work.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>422</td><td><code>validation_failed</code> · <code>unknown_fields</code> · <code>invalid_fields</code> · <code>invalid_filter</code> · <code>invalid_scope</code> · <code>scope_required</code> · <code>events_required</code> · <code>invalid_url</code> · <code>private_url</code></td><td>Field-level, scope or webhook URL problems — <code>details.errors[]</code> names listing validation issues.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>429</td><td><code>rate_limited</code> · <code>too_many_concurrent</code> · <code>global_write_limit</code> · <code>ip_locked</code></td><td>Back off for <code>Retry-After</code> seconds, then resume.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="ep-discovery">
        <h3 class="form-section"><span class="m-chip m-get">GET</span>&nbsp; <code>/api/v1</code> — discovery</h3>
        <p class="muted">Returns the API name, version, endpoint list and live limits. <b>Requires a key.</b> Handy for printing the surface a client supports.</p>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">curl</span>curl <%= SITE %>/api/v1 -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key"</div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="ep-health">
        <h3 class="form-section"><span class="m-chip m-get">GET</span>&nbsp; <code>/api/v1/health</code> — liveness</h3>
        <p class="muted">Liveness probe — returns a 200 and no business data. Still <b>authenticated</b>: it needs a key like everything else, so the status monitor carries one via <code>STATUS_API_KEY</code>.</p>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">curl</span>curl <%= SITE %>/api/v1/health -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key"</div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="ep-usage">
        <h3 class="form-section"><span class="m-chip m-get">GET</span>&nbsp; <code>/api/v1/usage</code> — usage dashboard data</h3>
        <p class="muted">Returns this account's current-calendar-month totals, writes, top endpoint aggregates and a trailing 31-day series. The <code>meta.current_key</code> object is the live rolling read/write budget for the key making the request.</p>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">curl</span>curl <%= SITE %>/api/v1/usage -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key"</div>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">shape</span>{
  <span class="k">"data"</span>: { <span class="k">"month_requests"</span>: <span class="s">1842</span>, <span class="k">"month_writes"</span>: <span class="s">17</span>, <span class="k">"top_endpoints"</span>: [ { <span class="k">"method"</span>: <span class="s">"GET"</span>, <span class="k">"endpoint"</span>: <span class="s">"/listings"</span>, <span class="k">"requests"</span>: <span class="s">1200</span> } ], <span class="k">"daily"</span>: [ { <span class="k">"day"</span>: <span class="s">"2026-09-04"</span>, <span class="k">"requests"</span>: <span class="s">42</span>, <span class="k">"writes"</span>: <span class="s">1</span> } ] },
  <span class="k">"meta"</span>: { <span class="k">"current_key"</span>: { <span class="k">"read"</span>: { <span class="k">"remaining"</span>: <span class="s">58</span> }, <span class="k">"write"</span>: { <span class="k">"remaining"</span>: <span class="s">20</span> } } }
}</div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="webhooks">
        <h3 class="form-section">Webhooks — push, not poll</h3>
        <p class="muted">Register one or more receiver URLs. FirmLedger queues a signed <code>POST</code> after a listing you own is approved, rejected, updated or deleted; when a listing is approved for the first time, subscribers to its category receive <code>listing.created</code>; and the verified owner receives <code>claim.verified</code>. Delivery happens after the API/admin request returns.</p>
        <table class="facts">
          <tr><th>Events</th><td><code>listing.approved</code> · <code>listing.rejected</code> · <code>listing.updated</code> · <code>listing.created</code> · <code>listing.deleted</code> · <code>claim.verified</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th>Filters</th><td><code>categories</code> is optional and filters the broadcast <code>listing.created</code> stream; a blank array receives every category. Owner lifecycle events are never hidden by a category filter.</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Authentication</th><td><code>manage:webhooks</code> scope. The signing secret is returned only from create/rotate — store it in your secret manager. Up to 10 receiver URLs per account.</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Retries</th><td>Timeouts, 408, 425, 429 and 5xx responses retry up to five attempts with backoff. Ten terminal failures pause a subscription automatically.</td></tr>
        </table>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">create</span>curl -X POST <%= SITE %>/api/v1/webhooks \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"label":"CRM production","url":"https://crm.example.com/hooks/firmledger","events":["listing.approved","listing.updated","claim.verified"],"categories":["Fintech"]}'</div>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">signed receiver headers</span>X-FirmLedger-Event: listing.approved
X-FirmLedger-Delivery: evt_…
X-FirmLedger-Timestamp: 1778000000
X-FirmLedger-Signature: v1=…
X-Idempotency-Key: evt_…</div>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">manage</span>curl <%= SITE %>/api/v1/webhooks/7/deliveries -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key"
curl -X POST <%= SITE %>/api/v1/webhooks/7/rotate-secret -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key"
curl -X POST <%= SITE %>/api/v1/webhooks/7/test -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key"</div>
        <p class="fine-print">Verify <code>HMAC_SHA256(timestamp + '.' + raw_request_body, secret)</code> and reject timestamps older than five minutes. Treat <code>X-Idempotency-Key</code> as the dedupe key — retries keep the same event id.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="ep-directory">
        <h3 class="form-section"><span class="m-chip m-get">GET</span>&nbsp; <code>/api/v1/listings</code> — company directory</h3>
        <p class="muted">Browse FirmLedger's <b>public, approved listings</b> with filters and pagination. <b>Requires a Pro key</b> and returns full profile fields, including contact details.</p>
        <table class="facts">
          <tr><th><code>page</code> · <code>per_page</code></th><td>Pagination — default <code>1</code> / <code>20</code>, max <code>50</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th><code>q</code></th><td>Free-text filter over name, tagline, description, tags, city &amp; category (part of the directory listing — there is no separate search endpoint)</td></tr>
          <tr><th><code>type</code> · <code>category</code> · <code>country</code> · <code>city</code> · <code>region</code></th><td>Filter by entity type, category name, country, city or region</td></tr>
          <tr><th><code>sponsored</code></th><td><code>1</code> to return only sponsored placements</td></tr>
          <tr><th><code>sort</code></th><td><code>featured</code> (default) · <code>newest</code> · <code>name</code> · <code>confidence</code> · <code>country</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th><code>fields</code></th><td>Optional comma-separated sparse fieldset, e.g. <code>fields=name,category,website</code>. <code>id</code> and <code>slug</code> are always retained.</td></tr>
        </table>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">curl</span>curl "<%= SITE %>/api/v1/listings?category=Fintech&amp;sort=newest&amp;per_page=50" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key"</div>
        <p class="fine-print">The key-gated legacy aliases <code>GET /api/v1/directory</code> and <code>GET /api/v1/directory/:slug</code> still work and return the same data — <code>/listings</code> is the canonical path.</p>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">200 OK</span>{
  <span class="k">"data"</span>: [ { <span class="k">"slug"</span>: <span class="s">"safiri-fintech"</span>, <span class="k">"name"</span>: <span class="s">"Safiri Fintech"</span>, <span class="k">"category"</span>: <span class="s">"Fintech"</span>, <span class="k">"confidence"</span>: <span class="s">72</span>, <span class="k">"email"</span>: <span class="s">"..."</span>, <span class="k">"url"</span>: <span class="s">".../listing/safiri-fintech"</span> } ],
  <span class="k">"meta"</span>: { <span class="k">"page"</span>: <span class="s">1</span>, <span class="k">"per_page"</span>: <span class="s">20</span>, <span class="k">"total"</span>: <span class="s">1</span>, <span class="k">"total_pages"</span>: <span class="s">1</span> }
}</div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="ep-profile">
        <h3 class="form-section"><span class="m-chip m-get">GET</span>&nbsp; <code>/api/v1/listings/:slug</code> — full company profile</h3>
        <p class="muted">Fetch a single approved listing by its <code>slug</code> — the full profile, with sources, technology radar and hiring link. Returns <code>404 not_found</code> if unknown or not yet approved. Add <code>?fields=name,category,website</code> when you only need a sparse response.</p>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">curl</span>curl <%= SITE %>/api/v1/listings/acme-logistics-ltd \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key"</div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="ep-create">
        <h3 class="form-section"><span class="m-chip m-post">POST</span>&nbsp; <code>/api/v1/listings</code> — create</h3>
        <p class="muted">Creates a record <b>you own</b> with status <code>pending</code> — it goes live after the standard moderation pass, exactly like dashboard submissions. Send JSON with <code>Content-Type: application/json</code>.</p>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table class="table">
            <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Rule</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>name</code> *</td><td>string</td><td>2–60 chars</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>tagline</code> *</td><td>string</td><td>20–90 chars — a proper one-liner</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>description</code> *</td><td>string</td><td>100–1200 chars</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>website</code> *</td><td>URL</td><td>Full URL — powers verification; one record per domain (409 on dupes)</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>country</code> *</td><td>string</td><td>e.g. "Kenya"</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>type</code></td><td>enum</td><td><%= limits.TYPES %></td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>category</code></td><td>string</td><td>Existing site category — new names are auto-registered</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>founded</code></td><td>string</td><td><code>2021</code> or <code>2021-07</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>size</code></td><td>enum</td><td><%= limits.SIZES %></td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>email</code> · <code>phone</code></td><td>string</td><td>Valid email / up to 40 chars</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>city</code> · <code>region</code> · <code>address</code></td><td>string</td><td>Length-capped free text</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>logo_url</code></td><td>URL</td><td>Direct image URL (logo storage is URL-based)</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>tags</code></td><td>array | string</td><td><code>["saas","fintech"]</code> or comma string — 160 chars total</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>socials</code></td><td>object</td><td>Keys from: <%= limits.SOCIALS %> — full URLs</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">curl</span>curl -X POST <%= SITE %>/api/v1/my/listings \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "name": "Acme Logistics Ltd",
    "tagline": "Cold-chain freight for East African exporters end to end",
    "description": "Acme Logistics Ltd runs refrigerated trucking and bonded warehousing between Mombasa, Nairobi and Kampala, giving exporters one audited cold chain from packhouse to airport.",
    "website": "https://acme-logistics.example",
    "country": "Kenya",
    "type": "company",
    "founded": "2019",
    "tags": ["logistics", "cold-chain"]
  }'</div>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">201 Created</span><span class="c"># Location: /api/v1/my/listings/42</span>
{
  <span class="k">"data"</span>: { <span class="k">"id"</span>: <span class="s">42</span>, <span class="k">"slug"</span>: <span class="s">"acme-logistics-ltd"</span>, <span class="k">"status"</span>: <span class="s">"pending"</span>, … },
  <span class="k">"meta"</span>: { <span class="k">"note"</span>: <span class="s">"Created with status "pending" — goes live after moderation…"</span> }
}</div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="ep-update">
        <h3 class="form-section"><span class="m-chip m-put">PUT</span>&nbsp; <code>/api/v1/listings/:id</code> — update</h3>
        <p class="muted">Send only the fields you want to change (any of the writable fields from POST). Unknown fields are rejected with <code>422 unknown_fields</code> so typos never silently drop. The response is the fully updated record. Only records you own.</p>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">curl</span>curl -X PUT <%= SITE %>/api/v1/listings/42 \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{ "tagline": "Cold-chain freight and bonded warehousing, Mombasa to Kampala", "city": "Mombasa" }'</div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="ep-delete">
        <h3 class="form-section"><span class="m-chip m-delete">DELETE</span>&nbsp; <code>/api/v1/listings/:id</code> — remove</h3>
        <p class="muted">Deletes the record and everything attached to it (events, jobs, watchlist stars, relationships) in one transaction. Returns <code>204 No Content</code>. Deleting is permanent — the same record can always be re-created. Only records you own.</p>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">curl</span>curl -X DELETE <%= SITE %>/api/v1/listings/42 -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key"
<span class="c"># → 204, empty body</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="ep-mine">
        <h3 class="form-section"><span class="m-chip m-get">GET</span>&nbsp; <code>/api/v1/my/listings</code> — your records</h3>
        <p class="muted">The records <b>you own</b>, paginated and filterable by status. This is where owner CRUD lives.</p>
        <table class="facts">
          <tr><th><code>page</code></th><td>Page number, default <code>1</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th><code>per_page</code></th><td>Page size, default <code>20</code>, max <code>50</code></td></tr>
          <tr><th><code>status</code></th><td>Optional: <code>pending</code>, <code>approved</code> or <code>rejected</code></td></tr>
        </table>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">curl</span>curl "<%= SITE %>/api/v1/my/listings?status=approved&amp;per_page=50" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key"</div>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">GET /api/v1/my/listings/:id</span><span class="c"># one of yours — full serialized record</span>
curl <%= SITE %>/api/v1/my/listings/42 -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key"</div>
        <p class="fine-print">Newest first. <code>meta</code> echoes page, per_page, total and total_pages.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="ep-categories">
        <h3 class="form-section"><span class="m-chip m-get">GET</span>&nbsp; <code>/api/v1/categories</code> — category list</h3>
        <p class="muted">Every category in the site tree, with its <code>slug</code>, whether it's official, and a live <code>listings_count</code> of approved records.</p>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">curl</span>curl <%= SITE %>/api/v1/categories -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key"</div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="ep-countries">
        <h3 class="form-section"><span class="m-chip m-get">GET</span>&nbsp; <code>/api/v1/countries</code> — country list</h3>
        <p class="muted">The distinct countries present in the approved ledger, each with its <code>listings_count</code>.</p>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">curl</span>curl <%= SITE %>/api/v1/countries -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key"</div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="ep-suggest">
        <h3 class="form-section"><span class="m-chip m-get">GET</span>&nbsp; <code>/api/v1/suggest</code> — autocomplete</h3>
        <p class="muted">Type-ahead suggestions for a search box: matching listings first, then categories, countries and cities. Each item carries a <code>type</code> so your UI can style it.</p>
        <table class="facts">
          <tr><th><code>q</code> *</th><td>Required prefix, up to 80 characters</td></tr>
          <tr><th><code>limit</code></th><td>Max items (default <code>8</code>, cap <code>25</code>)</td></tr>
        </table>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">curl</span>curl "<%= SITE %>/api/v1/suggest?q=fintech" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key"</div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="ep-verify">
        <h3 class="form-section"><span class="m-chip m-get">GET</span>&nbsp; <code>/api/v1/verify/domain/:domain</code> — check if listed</h3>
        <p class="muted">Check whether a domain is already on the ledger. Accepts a bare domain (<code>acme.com</code>) or a full URL, normalises it, and returns <code>listed</code>, the resolved <code>domain</code>, the matching <code>listing</code> (if any) and all <code>matches</code>.</p>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">curl</span>curl <%= SITE %>/api/v1/verify/domain/acme-logistics.example \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key"</div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="ep-export">
        <h3 class="form-section"><span class="m-chip m-get">GET</span>&nbsp; <code>/api/v1/export/listings.csv</code> — bulk export (Pro)</h3>
        <p class="muted">Download the approved ledger as a CSV. <b>Pro only.</b> Optional <code>category</code>, <code>country</code> and <code>type</code> filters narrow the row set. The response is <code>text/csv</code> with a <code>Content-Disposition: attachment</code> header.</p>
        <table class="facts">
          <tr><th><code>category</code> · <code>country</code> · <code>type</code></th><td>Optional filters</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Columns</th><td>id, slug, name, tagline, description, type, category, website, email, phone, country, city, region, address, logo_url, founded, size, tags, confidence, status, claimed, featured, sponsored, url, created_at, updated_at</td></tr>
        </table>
        <div class="code-block"><span class="code-label">curl</span>curl "<%= SITE %>/api/v1/export/listings.csv?country=Kenya" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer fl_live_your_key" \
  --output firmledger-listings.csv</div>
      </div>

      <div class="form-card docs-anchor" id="etiquette">
        <h3 class="form-section">Fair-use rules</h3>
        <p class="muted">The API is lenient by design and strict only where abuse starts. Integrations that follow these rules never see a limit:</p>
        <table class="facts">
          <tr><th>Retry with the clock</th><td>On <code>429</code>, wait <code>Retry-After</code> seconds — not a fixed blind loop</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Serial writes</th><td>Fire writes one after another, not in bursts — the concurrency gate rejects pile-ups</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Cache reads</th><td>Records change slowly; re-fetch on demand, not on a spin</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Keep keys server-side</th><td>Never ship a key in browser/mobile code — proxy through your backend</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Versioning</th><td><code>v1</code> is production-ready and stable — response shapes, error codes and field names are frozen. Breaking changes ship only as <code>/api/v2</code>, and v1 keeps working</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

